  "database": "rschema_0399",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0399 database is designed to manage user accounts, code submissions, problems, and projects. At its core, the database contains a table called \"user\" which stores information about each registered user, including their unique identifier, username, password, email, registration time, and personal details. The \"code\" table is used to store code submissions, each identified by a unique code ID, and linked to the user who submitted it, the problem it was submitted for, and the time of submission. The \"problem\" table contains details about each problem, including its unique identifier, name, description, difficulty level, and creation time. The \"project\" table stores information about each project, including its unique identifier, name, description, creation time, and the user who created it. The \"sign-in\" table tracks each time a user signs in, recording their unique identifier, sign-in time, and date. The \"user_participation_in_project\" table links users to the projects they participate in, including the project's difficulty level. Each of these tables is linked together through foreign keys, ensuring that a user can only submit code for a problem they exist, a user can only create a project if they have an account, and a user can only participate in a project if they exist and the project exists.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description:\nThe following describes a programming learning and project management system. The main functionalities of the system may include:\n1.User Management: Users can register, log in, and modify personal information. Each user has a User ID, Username, Password, Email, Registration Time, and Personal Information.\n2.Code Management: Users can upload, edit, and view code. The code includes Code ID, Code Content, Upload Time, and Problem ID.\n3.Problem Management: The system provides programming problems, including Problem ID, Problem Name, Problem Description, Difficulty Level, and Creation Time. Users can view and submit answers.\n4.Project Management: Each project includes Project ID, Project Name, Project Description, and Creation Time. Users can create, edit, and view projects.\n5.Sign-In Functionality: Records the sign-in status of each user, including Sign-In ID, User ID, Sign-In Time, and Sign-In Date. Users can sign in daily, and the system records the sign-in information.\nThere is a many-to-many relationship between Users and Codes, Users and Problems, and Users and Projects. The User table has a one-to-many relationship with the Sign-In table.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0399.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0399\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `personal_details` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `code` (\n  `code_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `problem_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `submission_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `code_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `code_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`problem_id`) REFERENCES `problem` (`problem_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `problem` (\n  `problem_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `difficulty_level` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`problem_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sign_in` (\n  `sign_in_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sign_in_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `sign_in_date` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sign_in_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sign_in_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_participation_in_project` (\n  `participation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `difficulty_level` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`participation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_participation_in_project_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_participation_in_project_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
